# Desktop UI Rules (Avalonia 12)

## Styling: tokens only
- Never hard-code colors, font sizes, spacing, radii, sizes, opacity or durations. Use tokens from `Styles/Tokens/`
  via `{DynamicResource ...}` (e.g. `BrushPrimary`, `BrushSurface`, `BrushTextMuted`, `FontSizeH3`, `Space4`,
  `RadiusLg`, `ShadowSm`, `ControlHeight`, `OpacityDisabled`). Full reference: `Docs/ui-foundation.md`.
- Brand 60-30-10: 60% `#FFFFFF`/`#EAF3FB` surfaces and background, 30% `#B7D6F0`/`#4A90C8` secondary,
  10% `#1F5A8A` primary accent. Never put normal-size text on `#4A90C8` (contrast too low).
- New colors go into `Styles/Tokens/Colors.axaml` in **both** the `Light` and `Dark` dictionaries; use semantic keys, not palette primitives.
- Text styles: `<TextBlock Classes="h2" />`, `caption`, `muted`, `strong`, `danger`...
- Button variants: `Classes="primary|secondary|danger|ghost|link"`, sizes `sm|lg`, icon-only `icon`.
- Icons: `<PathIcon Data="{StaticResource IconEdit}" />` from `Styles/Tokens/Icons.axaml`.

## Localization + RTL
- No user-visible literal text in views or components: use `{l:Tr Key}` (`xmlns:l="using:Mostawsef.Desktop.Services.Local"`),
  `{l:Tr Key, Arg=Property}` for a bound `{0}`, or `{l:TrKey Property}` when the view model holds the key.
- View models expose resource keys and never subscribe to `LanguageChanged`. `LocalizationService` comes from DI;
  controls use `App.Localization` (subscribe on attach, unsubscribe on detach). No static `Instance`.
- Every new key goes into **both** `Resources/Strings.resx` (English) and `Resources/Strings.ar.resx` (Arabic).
- Layout mirrors automatically in Arabic. Think "start/end": do not flip margins or alignment manually per language.
- Theme/language switches: use `ui:PreferencesBar`; do not add toggle commands to view models.
- Every new `Window` must call `App.Localization.Apply(window)`.

## Responsiveness
- Breakpoints on the AppShell content width (container `AppContent`), not the window: Compact < 900, Medium < 1280,
  Wide < 1600, XWide >= 1600. Values live in `Styles/Tokens/Breakpoints.axaml`; keep `Styles/Responsive.axaml` in sync.
- Page roots use `Classes="page"` (page padding, content capped at `ContentMaxWidth`). Use `ui:ResponsiveGrid` for card/form
  grids and utility classes `hide-compact|show-compact|stack-compact|hide-medium|show-medium|hide-wide|show-wide`.
- No fixed widths/heights on page content; let it stretch and wrap. Text that can be long gets `TextWrapping` or `TextTrimming`.
- The sidebar collapses to icons below `AppShell.AutoCompactWidth` (1100). The window has `WindowMinWidth`/`WindowMinHeight`
  (720 x 520): every page must stay usable at that size, in both languages.
- Layout must work at Compact width: test new pages with a narrow headless window when the layout changes per breakpoint.

## MVVM + bindings
- Compiled bindings are on: every view/DataTemplate needs `x:DataType`.
- View models derive from `ViewModelBase`, use `[ObservableProperty] public partial T Name { get; set; }` and `[RelayCommand]`.
- Services come from DI (`ServiceRegistration.AddMostawsefDesktop`); register new services there. Page view models are registered from `AppRoutes`.
- Dialogs: `DialogService.ShowAsync(modal)` / `ConfirmAsync(...)`. Notifications: `ToastService.Show(...)`.
- API calls go in `Services/Api/` (one `<Feature>Api` class through `ApiClient`) using DTOs from `Mostawsef.Contracts`.
  `ApiClient` never throws for HTTP failures: it returns `ApiResult<T>` with an `ApiError`
  (`Unreachable|Unauthorized|Forbidden|BadRequest|NotFound|Conflict|TooManyRequests|Server`). View models map each relevant error to a resource key.

## Validation (desktop)
- The server is the source of truth; the desktop only checks what makes a request pointless (empty required fields, obvious format).
- Disable the submit command via `CanExecute` until required fields are filled; show per-field messages with `ui:FormField Error`
  (a resource key from the view model) and the server's 400/409 outcome as a form error or toast.
- Do not duplicate business rules (uniqueness, allowed states) on the desktop.

## State
- **Session** (`SessionService`): user, role and token in memory only; cleared on sign-out or a 401.
- **Preferences** (`SettingsService` -> `%AppData%/Mostawsef/settings.json`): only `Theme`, `Language`, `ApiBaseUrl`.
  Never write tokens, passwords, user data or medical data to disk.
- **Theme** (`ThemeService`) and **language** (`LocalizationService`) are app-wide singletons that save to settings; change them only through `ui:PreferencesBar`.
- **Page state** lives in its view model. Services are singletons; page view models are transient (fresh per navigation).
  No static mutable state.

## Auth + navigation (see `Docs/auth.md`)
- Every screen is listed in `AppRoutes` (view, access, portal menus); open pages only via `NavigationService` or the shell menu.
- New portal pages: view model + view under `ViewModels|Views/<Role>/`, then one `.Page<Vm, View>(icon, titleKey)` line in the role's portal in `AppRoutes`.
- All roles share one `PortalShellViewModel` + `Views/Shell/PortalShellView`; a role's title and menu come from its `AppRoutes` portal. Never subclass the shell per role.
- Never store tokens or passwords on disk; the session lives in `SessionService` memory.
